{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"13 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,51.364,3.651,3.268,"Paytm (One 97 Communications)"],[13.889,14.731,36.475,2.373,2.124,"A full price for a fee without a start date"],[13.889,20.845,52.964,1.809,1.634,"Paytm is at a 52-week high after two regulatory gifts. On 15 September NPCI"],[13.889,22.289,52.951,1.809,1.634,"allowed a merchant fee (MDR) of up to 0.4% on UPI payments above ₹2,000,"],[13.889,23.733,52.936,1.809,1.634,"and today the RBI approved in principle the return of the wallet. Management"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"puts the MDR uplift at 2.5bp of GMV, about ₹710 cr a year against annualised"],[13.889,26.621,52.934,1.809,1.634,"H1 EBITDA of ₹946 cr. Yet the start date, moved from 15 October to “after"],[13.889,28.065,52.951,1.809,1.634,"Diwali”, is still not notified and the fee is under challenge in the Supreme Court."],[13.889,29.509,52.277,1.809,1.634,"Q2 FY27 was strong: revenue rose 28% to ₹2,648 cr and EBITDA was ₹270 cr."],[13.889,31.995,52.992,1.809,1.634,"1) GMV grows 27%, 22% and 20% in FY27-29E. 2) MDR starts on 1 January"],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"2027 at half the guided rate, then 2.5bp, all reaching EBITDA (₹921 cr in"],[13.889,34.883,52.962,1.809,1.634,"FY28E). 3) Default-loss guarantees resume with the largest lender, cutting"],[13.889,36.328,52.936,1.809,1.634,"contribution margin from 56% to 53% in Q3. 4) Indirect costs grow half as fast"],[13.889,37.772,52.959,1.809,1.634,"as contribution profit. EPS is then ₹17.3, ₹40.4 and ₹57.4 for FY27-29E"],[13.889,39.216,52.931,1.809,1.634,"(consensus ₹18.9 and ₹39.9). Without MDR, FY28E EPS is ₹26.5. Paytm also"],[13.889,40.684,52.936,1.809,1.634,"pays tax only on interest income: ₹7,792 cr of old losses shelter operating profit"],[13.889,42.128,30.893,1.809,1.634,"until FY30E. Fully taxed, FY28E EPS is ₹32.5."],[13.889,44.59,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹1,620 averages two methods. A 48x P/E, midway between"],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"the 59x paid today and the 37x median of PB Fintech, Pine Labs, Groww and"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"MobiKwik, on fully-taxed forward EPS of ₹42.2, plus ₹17 of remaining tax"],[13.889,48.946,52.966,1.809,1.634,"shield, gives ₹2,040. A ten-year DCF (12% cost of equity, 5.5% terminal"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"growth) plus cash gives ₹1,200. The price needs operating profit to grow 32% a"],[13.889,51.834,52.951,1.809,1.634,"year in FY30-36E; we assume 25% fading to 10%. MDR is ₹460 of our target."],[13.889,53.278,52.987,1.809,1.634,"We rate the shares Underweight (ladder: −5% to +15%). Upside risks: platform"],[13.889,54.722,52.032,1.809,1.634,"fees, the wallet, buybacks. Downside: an adverse court ruling, guarantee losses."],[13.889,57.21,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,66.579,1.489,1.022,0.915,"800"],[14.451,65.277,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,000"],[14.451,63.965,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,200"],[14.451,62.665,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,400"],[14.451,61.363,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,600"],[14.451,60.051,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,800"],[14.451,58.751,2.306,1.022,0.915,"2,000"],[18.306,67.273,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.929,67.273,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.701,67.273,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.473,67.273,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.699,68.444,3.122,1.275,1.111,"Paytm ("],[21.824,68.47,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.437,68.444,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.52,68.444,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.291,69.604,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.561,69.604,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.279,69.604,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,69.604,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,70.67,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.372,70.67,2.811,1.387,1.209,"49.3%"],[24.09,70.67,2.811,1.387,1.209,"13.1%"],[28.808,70.67,2.811,1.387,1.209,"17.6%"],[33.527,70.67,2.811,1.387,1.209,"48.